# SAFi Appliance — packages baked into the live rootfs.
#
# ONLY daemon-free packages live here. Anything whose postinst starts a daemon
# (mysql-server, apache2, openssh-server) is installed by
# config/hooks/normal/010-* AFTER a policy-rc.d that blocks service starts —
# otherwise the build chroot tries to run systemd daemons it has no boot for.
#
# Everything SAFi actually needs at runtime:
#   python3-venv         → virtualenv (DEPLOY_BAREMETAL.md step 4)
#   gcc g++              → a few Python wheels build from source
#   tesseract-ocr-eng    → OCR for image/PDF attachments (Dockerfile ships it)
#   nodejs npm           → npx MCP tool servers (Dockerfile ships Node 22)
#   git                  → waters the repo during PHP-style upgrades (step 10)
#   openssh-server       → operator console access (installed in 010-hook)
# Plus the live system needs a kernel/init and tools; live-build supplies the
# base. These are the additions:
apt-utils
bash
ca-certificates
curl
debconf-utils
dnsutils
g++
gcc
git
hostname
ifupdown
less
live-tools
login
mawk
nano
nodejs
npm
passwd
procps
psmisc
python3-venv
sudo
tesseract-ocr
tesseract-ocr-eng